<title>BELGIUM: REAL SOFTWARE TO FLOAT ON BOURSE IN JUNE-NEWSPAPER.</title>
<headline>REAL SOFTWARE TO FLOAT ON BOURSE IN JUNE-NEWSPAPER.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Antwerp computer firm Real Software will float 38 percent of its share capital, or around 450,000 shares, on the Brussels bourse in June, De Financieel Economische Tijd newspaper said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It said the float price would be set later.</p>
<p>Real Software, created in 1986, has an income of 1.2 billion francs and a pre-tax profit of 180 million francs.</p>
<p>The newspaper said it had an annual growth rate of 15 to 20 percent.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
